{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"advisory":[{"block_threshold":0.5,"blocking_enabled":true,"carried_from":"prior finding 0","criteria":["error-handling","correctness"],"decision":"advisory","evidence":["_observability_harness.py:113-114: `_kill_group(proc.pid)` then `proc.communicate()` with no timeout","The docstring motivation (commit message) is that stock-macOS runs waited on the real daemon unbounded; a D-state child blocks the uncapped reap the same way"],"finding":"On the timeout/interrupt path, after killing the process group with SIGKILL, run_observability calls proc.communicate() with no timeout. If any process in the group fails to terminate promptly (e.g. a child in uninterruptible D-state waiting on the host Docker daemon or a stuck mount), this second communicate() blocks indefinitely, defeating the very timeout bound the harness exists to enforce.","id":"3","impact":0.0,"location":"tests/scripts/_observability_harness.py:113","norm_id":"n9ed19155e7c0d56a","priority":0.0,"reason":"default-advisory","standing":{"origin_decision":"advisory","origin_revision":"8e27f801221e621c475fad56ddf71befc8c1f9f8","state":"still-present"},"suggested_fix":"Pass a finite timeout to the reaping communicate() (e.g. proc.communicate(timeout=5)) and let a secondary TimeoutExpired surface rather than block forever.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.7143,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"na","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","respects_artifact_altitude":"na","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"blast_radius":"local","capability_degraded":false,"churn90":0,"contract_drift":false,"data_loss_without_recovery":false,"dead_code":false,"debt_impact":"low","escapes_automation":true,"forbids_contract_allowed_state":false,"hard_to_reverse_surface":false,"hidden_invariant":false,"implicit_coupling":false,"likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reachable_path_without_automated_coverage":false,"removed_public_symbol":false,"reversibility":"easy","safety_net_removal_without_replacement":false,"security_bypass_not_enforced_elsewhere":false,"silent_failure":false,"silent_wrong_feeding_a_decision":false,"trigger_likelihood":"rare","unversioned_published_contract_break":false,"version_signal_present":false}}},{"block_threshold":0.5,"blocking_enabled":true,"carried_from":"prior finding 1","criteria":["error-handling","edge-cases"],"decision":"advisory","evidence":["test_observability_harness_isolation.py:155-170: hits only when `any(_names_script(item, ...) for item in _argv_items(node.args[0]))`, and _argv_items only unpacks ast.List/ast.Tuple else returns [argv]","_names_script returns True only for an ast.Name whose id is in script_names or str(Name); a variable holding the argv list is an ast.Name bound to a List, which is not in script_names","The anti-vacuity test only exercises the inline-list form (test_sample.py:4), so the aliased-argv gap is uncovered"],"finding":"The AST guard _direct_script_runs only flags a subprocess call whose FIRST argument is a literal list/tuple (or str()) that textually contains the SCRIPT name. A test that binds the argv to a variable first (cmd = [\"bash\", str(SCRIPT)]; subprocess.run(cmd, ...)) runs the script directly yet is invisible to the scan, so the isolation guarantee fails open for that pattern.","id":"4","impact":0.225,"location":"tests/scripts/test_observability_harness_isolation.py:168","norm_id":"nfdf04e9b09738ad4","priority":0.225,"reason":